        "id": "ch6_3-1",
        "text": "The Xfce Desktop Interface\nWhile the GNOME 3, KDE Plasma, Cinnamon, and MATE desktops are very fancy,\nthey all require quite a bit of computing resources to operate. One of the original\nselling points of Linux is that it could run on just about any old PC you had laying\naround. Unfortunately, with those desktops, that\u2019s not always the case.\nHowever, other graphical desktop environments are less resource-intensive, and\ncan indeed run on just about anything. The Xfce desktop is one such desktop. This\nsection explores the features of the Xfce desktop, and shows how you can custom-\nize it.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 History of Xfce\n\u2022 The Whisker menu\n\u2022 Changing Xfce settings\n\u2022 Applets\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
